<p>Students at several Iranian universities staged fresh anti-government protests as the new term began. Reports said they chanted slogans and, in some cases, marched on campus. At some campuses, demonstrators clashed with pro-government groups, underlining how tense university life remains after weeks of unrest. The rallies also aligned with 40-day mourning ceremonies traditionally held for people killed in last month’s nationwide demonstrations. Those protests were met with a deadly crackdown that reports describe as leaving thousands dead.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/w6_FAUql1xkq9Gc2-OZysoadr0Rzj5-llbCZuRKumkIfULPtBVVQSE34FMY2MDQt-Y__hfDSs2uhZrvRbJwdMimpaRTCSChYm710bVhAaRzgOzK04cu2ctQ3UbWp1OVXngfOWRf-FTWUPmNkld1get9GOWvPjfUX9LgzmD-WBoDIcujbcLcEJCR1vN_ixzKKeMSXG0GiVu0' alt='Demonstrators gather at Amirkabir University in Tehran, in a social media image verified by The New York Times.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>First large return: BBC described the campus rallies as the first large anti-government student protests since last month’s deadly crackdown.</li><li>Counter-protesters on campus: Reuters reporting cited by Al-Monitor said pro-government groups confronted students at some universities, suggesting organized pushback inside campus spaces.</li><li>Information flow: Much of what is known about the demonstrations came from videos and posts shared online and amplified by diaspora media, reflecting how hard it is to report on campus protests under tight security.</li><li>Scale of the wider unrest: Reuters described last month’s demonstrations as the worst domestic unrest since Iran’s 1979 Islamic Revolution.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Student protesters: As universities reopened, demonstrators chanted anti-government slogans and held campus marches. BBC described the protests as acts of remembrance for those killed in last month’s crackdown. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5yj2kzkrj0o'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>Iranian authorities and pro-government groups: State-linked outlets cited in reports described confrontations at several universities, with pro-government groups facing off against student protesters. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/iranian-students-begin-new-university-term-protests'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>US government (Trump administration): Coverage says the Trump administration has stepped up US military deployments in the region while pressing Iran to accept terms for a new nuclear deal, including a time-bound push referenced by some outlets. (<a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/iran-on-edge-campus-protests-erupt-against-khamenei-regime-amid-us-war-fears-13982338.html'>Firstpost</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/21/world/middleeast/iran-student-protests.html'>Iran’s Students Hold Anti-Regime Protests as Universities Reopen</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/iran-on-edge-campus-protests-erupt-against-khamenei-regime-amid-us-war-fears-13982338.html'>Iran on edge: Campus protests erupt against Khamenei regime amid US war fears</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iranian-students-chant-anti-government-slogans-as-us-threats-loom/article70662466.ece'>Iranian students chant anti-government slogans, as U.S. threats loom</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5yj2kzkrj0o'>Iran students stage first large anti-government protests since deadly crackdown</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/iranian-students-begin-new-university-term-protests'>Iranian students begin new university term with protests</a> - al-monitor.com</li></ul>